{
  "_comment": [
    "Virtual enzyme-activity panel, one entry per BPS Bioscience biochemical",
    "screening family. Targets are pinned by UniProt accession, not by name or",
    "by ChEMBL ID typed from memory: the ChEMBL target record is resolved from",
    "the accession at run time and must come back as SINGLE PROTEIN.",
    "",
    "That indirection is the fix for the failure mode the 3CLpro work hit, where",
    "CHEMBL4523582 turned out to be the whole pp1ab polyprotein and mixed Mpro,",
    "PLpro and RdRp assays into one record - 19% of labels belonged to a",
    "different protein. Pinning to a single-protein accession makes that class of",
    "contamination impossible rather than something to be caught by keyword",
    "filtering afterwards.",
    "",
    "controls are used only for post-hoc recall validation (does the virtual",
    "assay rank the real assay's reference inhibitors as potent?). They are NOT",
    "removed from training and NOT used for model selection."
  ],
  "chembl_version_note": "Resolved at run time; the version actually used is recorded in results/panel_provenance.json",
